Package: buildwright
Title: Dependency-Health and Build-Failure Diagnostics for Managed R
    Environments
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Amit", "Shenoy", , "shenoy.am@husky.neu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Diagnoses dependency health and predicts build and install
    failures for large, managed R package distributions of the kind
    maintained on Posit Connect, Posit Workbench, and Bioconductor. It
    scans installed libraries and 'renv' lockfiles, builds a dependency
    graph, detects version conflicts and cycles, maps packages to their
    system requirements, and simulates installation order to surface
    failures before an install is attempted. Results can be rendered as a
    static report or explored in an interactive dashboard, and the checks
    can be wired into 'renv' and 'pak' workflows as a pre-install hook.
License: GPL-3
